body:
An `image` field declares optional path options. `roots:` names the root set the field's path points at: `assets`, the deck's `assets/` tree, or `media`, the `media/` tree of the library layer that owns the field's template (solution.note.variants-from-load-expansion); with no `roots`, the path resolves under the deck's `assets/`. `dir:` optionally restricts the path to a subdirectory within a root, and `extensions:` optionally restricts it to a set of allowed file-name extensions. The path is existence-checked at validation time against the declared roots: it must name an existing file in a declared root, resolved against the roots in their written order, and a path that names no such file is a validation error carrying the offending path and a closest-match suggestion over the candidate files the field accepts — the existing files within the declared roots, under `dir` when set, with an allowed extension when `extensions` is set (e.g. bg: no such file "bgs/right-88.jpg" - did you mean "bgs/right-8.jpg"?). A layout receives the resolved URL for the field: for a `media` root it is the same URL the layout `media` helper produces for the owning layer's `media/` (requirements.constraint.media-paths-library-relative), and for an `assets` root it is the deck `assets/` image URL.

AC:
- an `image` field declaring `roots: [media]` with a value naming an existing file under the owning library layer's `media/` validates and its value renders as the same URL the layout `media` helper produces;
- an `image` field declaring `roots: [assets]`, or declaring no `roots`, validates a path under the deck's `assets/`;
- a value naming no file in a declared root fails validation with a closest-match suggestion over the candidate files the field accepts;
- `dir:` restricts the accepted path to a subdirectory of a root, and `extensions:` restricts it to the listed file-name extensions;
- a path under a declared `media` root resolves in the layer that owns the field's template (library-layer-references).
